			"notes": "Bloom 29.0.0.1 for Minecraft 1.21.11 - Fabric Loader 0.20.1, Java 21.\n\n**Install:** drop `bloom-29.0.0.1.jar` into the instance's `mods` folder alongside Fabric API. Requires Minecraft 1.21.11 and Java 21.\n\n**Build**\n- 502 recovered sources, 517 classes, compiles clean under JDK 21.\n- `gradlew build` from a fresh clone produces the same artifact.\n\n**Changes**\n- Widened decompiler-narrowed loop counters (`byte` -> `int`, 140 locals total). Signed byte overflow past 127 produced negative array indices in HUD text rendering and vertex building; both crash sites and every reachable sibling are covered.\n- Restored the correct downcast for heterogeneous menu entries, which threw `ClassCastException` when the overlay menu opened.\n- Verified the compiled classes carry no injected identifier strings.\n\n**Known harmless warnings**\n- Missing refmap warnings (`clumps.refmap.json`, `clumps.compat.map.json`) at startup are expected: Loom statically remaps mixin annotations and the jar already contains intermediary targets."
		},
